<p>A denied insurance claim in Corpus Christi can feel final, especially after weeks of waiting for an answer. In practice, denials are based on specific reasons: a policy exclusion, a finding about the cause of damage, a question about timing, or missing information. Some of those reasons hold up. Others rest on an incomplete inspection or a misreading of the facts. As a Corpus Christi Public Adjuster, we review the denial letter, the policy, and the property to help you understand whether the denial is supported and what options may remain.</p>

<h2>Common Reasons Claims Are Denied</h2>
<p>Denial letters usually cite one or more policy provisions. The table below lists reasons we often see on Coastal Bend claims and the kind of evidence that may respond to each. Every claim is different, and some denials are correct under the policy.</p>
